# Consistent line endings for everyone.
#
# Why this exists: contributors may be on Windows while CI runs on Linux.
# Without this rule, git rewrites line endings every time a file moves between
# machines. That shows up as noisy "warning: LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# messages and slowly turns into fake diffs that make PR review harder.
#
# Reproducibility of the submission file does NOT depend on this file: the CSV
# is written with `newline=""` and `lineterminator="\n"` in `submit.py`, so the
# result is identical on Windows and Linux. This is about day-to-day peace of
# mind.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that really are binary -- git must never touch them.
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
